; LAUNCH/AWAIT/YIELD: MultiLogo-style concurrent turtle agents.
;
; LAUNCH "procname spawns a fresh turtle running that (zero-input)
; procedure as its own independent agent. YIELD hands control to the
; other running agents instead of running this one to completion in a
; single burst. AWAIT blocks the caller until every launched agent has
; finished.
;
; The scheduler is headless and synchronous, so the canvas only
; repaints once everything below is done -- what proves the three
; agents genuinely interleaved (rather than one running start-to-finish
; before the next even starts) is that all three polygons come out
; whole and correctly shaped despite each one only taking a single step
; at a time before yielding to the other two.

TO polygon :sides :length :start_x :start_y
  PENUP
  SETXY :start_x :start_y
  PENDOWN
  REPEAT :sides [
    FD :length
    RT (360 / :sides)
    YIELD
  ]
END

TO triangle
  SETPENCOLOR 220 40 40
  polygon 3 90 120 350
END

TO square
  SETPENCOLOR 40 140 220
  polygon 4 70 250 380
END

TO hexagon
  SETPENCOLOR 40 180 90
  polygon 6 50 380 350
END

LAUNCH "triangle
LAUNCH "square
LAUNCH "hexagon
AWAIT

PRINT "all-agents-done
